@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# ClaudeProtect integration changes (2026-10-29)
+
+These changes were made while integrating Core with ClaudeProtect. Public LEPB v4 and `LEP_RUNTIME_ENVIRONMENT` layouts are unchanged.
+
+## Changes
+
+- `Hooks/NtdllHook.cpp`
+  - Handle `SystemDynamicTimeZoneInformation` in `LepNtQuerySystemInformation`, returning the configured `RTL_DYNAMIC_TIME_ZONE_INFORMATION`. The key name comes from `LepGlobalData::ConfiguredTimezoneId`.
+  - In virtual MUI mode, override `RtlGetThreadPreferredUILanguages` results with the configured culture when `MUI_LANGUAGE_ID`/`MUI_LANGUAGE_NAME` is requested.
+- `Hooks/Kernel32Hook.cpp`
+  - Add `GetACP`/`GetOEMCP` export hooks returning the configured code pages. PEB/ntdll synchronization alone did not cover `GetACP` on this build.
+  - Add `GetUserPreferredUILanguages`/`GetSystemPreferredUILanguages` export hooks returning the configured culture. The size query (`LanguagesBuffer == nullptr`) returns TRUE with the required length; an undersized buffer returns FALSE with `ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER`.
+  - Install the existing `GetUserDefaultUILanguage`/`GetSystemDefaultUILanguage` export hooks for `HookUILanguageMode >= 1`, so mode 2 also covers those exports.
+- `LocaleEmulatorPlus.cpp`
+  - Read `CP_TIMEZONE` into `ConfiguredTimezoneId` at initialization. This is an integration input from the launcher, not a public ABI change.
+- `LocaleEmulatorPlus.h`
+  - Add `ConfiguredTimezoneId[128]` to `LepGlobalData`; add preferred-language hook typedefs and stubs.
+- `support/native/Runtime.h`
+  - Add `RTL_DYNAMIC_TIME_ZONE_INFORMATION` with a 432-byte layout assertion.
+
+## Why
+
+Chromium/Electron and ICU use `GetDynamicTimeZoneInformation`, which was not virtualized by the `SystemCurrentTimeZoneInformation` case. Chromium language/navigator behavior required both the Win32 UI-language exports and `--lang`; preferred-language queries otherwise returned the host list. `GetACP`/`GetOEMCP` returned host values despite PEB/ntdll synchronization in the tested build.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `scripts/build-lep.ps1 -Test` passed all four upstream suites.
+- Native probe: UTC/en-US and Tokyo/ja-JP both pass time zone (static and dynamic), locale, ACP/OEMCP, UI language, preferred languages, Job membership and LEP initialization.
+- Chromium/Edge proxy under LEP: renderer and Worker report UTC/en-US and Asia/Tokyo/ja-JP as configured; `--lang` supplies the Chromium language switch.
+- Claude Desktop process tree under LEP: main, crashpad, GPU, utility and renderers are in the Job; LEP injection/log evidence is present; Stop, main exit and supervisor kill leave no processes.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- `CP_TIMEZONE` is required for dynamic time-zone key names. Without it the dynamic case returns the configured bias/names but an empty key name; launchers that need `GetDynamicTimeZoneInformation().TimeZoneKeyName` must set it.
+- The preferred-language export hooks return a single configured language; host fallback chains are intentionally removed inside the virtualized process.
+- `GetSystemDefaultLocaleName`/system LCID are not changed.
