@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Electron language virtualization
+
+With `HookUILanguageMode=2`, Core virtualizes the Win32 user, system and thread preferred UI-language lists and the `Languages` property of `Windows.System.UserProfile.GlobalizationPreferences` requested through `IGlobalizationPreferencesStatics`.
+
+Electron 44.9.3 first reads this WinRT property for `app.getPreferredSystemLanguages()`, then falls back to a merged thread UI-language list. Hooking only the user/system Win32 exports leaves its first-choice path on host languages. See [Electron's implementation](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v44.9.3/shell/common/language_util_win.cc).
+
+`Hooks/WinrtHook.cpp` hooks `combase!RoGetActivationFactory` after combase initialization, including lazy loads through the existing module notification mechanism. Only the exact class/interface pair is wrapped. The wrapper owns the original factory reference, implements IUnknown/IInspectable lifetime, returns an immutable single-language `IVectorView<HSTRING>`, and delegates the other globalization properties to the original object. Other classes and requested interfaces remain untouched; the newer per-user globalization interface is not virtualized by this wrapper.
+
+String and COM allocator exports are resolved dynamically. Core remains manually mapped and introduces no combase import into bootstrap. The public LEPB v4 layout is unchanged. Mode 0/1 do not install these preferred-language/WinRT hooks.
+
+ClaudeProtect's independent probe covers the same WinRT Size/GetAt path as Electron, plus IndexOf, GetMany, bounds and HSTRING ownership, for parent and child processes. Matching x86 and x64 loaders pass en-US; x64 also passes ja-JP. These probe results are not direct evidence of Claude's rendered interface or a guarantee about an application's saved language override.
